      - Definitions: {"Movies_and_TV:scope": "One frozen category model, public training histories and targets only; targets may have influenced fitting. No additional scorer, checkpoint or ensemble is fitted or loaded.", "Movies_and_TV:identity": "Cache at most ten batches; uniquely match encoded prefix plus aligned target against public training endpoints. Deterministic seed-42 shuffle of eligible user IDs, cap 32, one event each; last eight selected users reserved for confirmation. Selection does not inspect scores or patch results.", "Movies_and_TV:candidates": "Diagnostic target plus up to 99 unique uniform alternatives excluding the target and every observed training-history item. Repeat targets are retained exactly once. IDs, shortage and degeneracy are in replay. These are not pinned host candidates; primary summaries require 99 negatives. At most ten candidates makes HR@10 degenerate.", "Movies_and_TV:outcome_vector": "Every outcome/delta vector is [raw target-minus-best-alternative margin, one-based target rank, diagnostic HR@10]. Descending computed FP32 scores, then ascending integer item ID; exact equality defines ties. Positive margin/hit change is better; positive rank change is worse.", "Movies_and_TV:stage1": "Three independent permutations of earlier occupied positions, with endpoint, padding and earlier-item multiset fixed. No rejection sampling. Identity inputs remain scheduled and have exactly zero input-intervention effect. Input effects are corrupted minus clean; corruption gap is clean minus corrupted.", "Movies_and_TV:stage2": "Every eligible draw is patched regardless of score responsiveness. One boundary after block floor(B/2)-1. Choose largest earlier occupied p with r-p in downstream offsets and p-i in upstream offsets for an earlier occupied input i. Patch the complete vector at p after residual addition/masking. Restoration is clean vector into corrupted input; disruption is corrupted vector into clean input. Each delta uses its own re